WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.180
In 1982, a new source of human
insulin was approved for use.

2
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.490
It came from bacteria,
grown in large fermenters,

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.830
then extracted and purified.

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.000
Before that, people relied on
insulin from pigs or cattle.

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.910
But bacteria don't make human hormones.

6
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.640
So how can a bacterium be made to
produce one it has never made before?

7
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.880
In this mission, you'll see that only a
small fraction of the cells in a culture

8
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.260
ever change.

9
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.630
Then you'll follow one
changed cell as it divides,

10
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.600
again and again, into a factory.

11
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: find out how a bacterium
can be made to produce a human hormone.
